===1963 to 1979===
In 1963, Ontario switched to a quarterly system for commercial plates. Plates could be issued on a quarterly basis rather than paying for a full year of registration.
<gallery>
File:Ontario 1963 Commercial quarterly plate expires March 1964.jpg|This 1963 Ontario commercial licence plate was the first quarterly plate. It expired in March 1964 and until dated March quarterly plates appeared in March 1967 this plate when issued in December 1963 was used as a quarterly commercial plate.
File:Ontario June 1965 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|In 1965 all June, September and December quarterly plates were issued in the reverse colours as in 1963 and 1964. In alternate years Ontario quarterly plates reversed their colours each year.
File:Ontario MAR 1967 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|First issue of commercial quarterly plates dated for March.
File:Ontario SEP 1969 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|Each plate would be valid for three months or a quarter of the year. This plate was issued in June 1969 and expired in September 1969.
File:Ontario DEC 1971 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|Quarterly plates had several serial format arrangements. Beginning in March 1968 they switched to the '''A'''1-234, 123-4'''A''' and '''A'''12-345 & 123-45'''A''' formats.
File:Ontario JUN 1974 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|
File:Ontario SEP 1976 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|
File:Ontario DEC 1978 QUARTERLY COMMERCIAL Plate.jpg|
File:Ontario Commercial Quarterly License Plate MAR-80 D96-082.jpg|Final quarterly plate issued. Ontario switched to plates renewed with stickers in 1980.
</gallery>

